<data>
# The worked example of project_format3.md section 9.1 on T2's levels (README.md): a thick-target yield curve of
# 15N(p,a0)12C across the resonances at E_lab = 1.01 and 1.04 MeV (T2's levels at E_x = 13.073 and 13.105 MeV),
# counted per uC of an H+ beam (charge state 1) with an efficiency x branching of 0.0182, on a thick (infinite) 15N
# target.  Synthetic data (make_story.py).  A layer of 13C with N fitted in the yield's prefactor, as the note writes it, is the layer
# kernel of Phase 5: this engine folds a layer into the target-averaged cross section (data_kinds.md eq. 2).
dataset Y_curve
    reaction       15N(p,a)12C
    quantity       yield
    unit           counts/uC
    charge_state   1
    efficiency     0.0182 fixed
    file           data/yield_curve.dat
    columns        E_lab[keV] _ value error
    norm           1 fit prior 1 3%
    target         N15T
    beam           pbeam
    quadrature     points 60
</data>
<extrapolations>
extrapolation Y_thick
    reaction       15N(p,a)12C
    quantity       yield
    unit           1/particle
    energies       range 0.6 1.4 MeV lab step 0.01
    target         N15T
    beam           pbeam
    quadrature     points 60
</extrapolations>
<targets>
target N15T
    kind           infinite
    active         15N
    composition    N 1
    stopping       formula "a0*x^a1" a0=4.5e-20 a1=-0.6 MeV*cm2/atom
    straggling     none
beam pbeam
    spread         0.3 keV lab
</targets>
